WEBVTT

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.830
They're late.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.950
Relax a little, Kei.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.080
These people would be late
for their own mother's funeral.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.200
I know. But I've got somewhere to be.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.540
Meeting a lady?

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.370
Yeah, she's gorgeous.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:49.620
A lovely blue-eyed brunette.
Every night she digs her nails into my skin.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.660
Oh, you mean Kuroi.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.250
Finally. There they are.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.450
Let's get to work, then.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.080
You got the cash, mister?

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.080
You shitheads are late.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.040
The cops could be by at any minute.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.290
The cash. Do you have it? Or not?

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.700
What about you? You got the stuff?

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.330
It's supposed to be good quality stuff, right?
Shipped straight from the source.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:17.000
Show us the money. Money first.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.700
You piece of shit...

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.200
Calm down.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.370
Look, here it is.
Fifty grand in cold, hard cash.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.500
Now show us the stuff.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.000
What do you think, mister?

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.580
A real fairy.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.200
Yeah, that's good quality, all right.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.410
Right, Kei?

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.790
A higher race, huh?

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:43.120
You could make some
really good drugs with this.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.540
Where'd you get it?

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.410
Afraid that's a trade secret, mister.

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:49.040
Whatever. We'll take it.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.500
--Rick.
--Right.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.660
Thanks for the business, mister. Thanks.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.700
Pleasure working with you guys.
Glad it worked out.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:06.540
I'm happy too.
Now we can finally get to the point.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.000
This is the San-Teresa Metropolitan Police.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.750
You're under arrest.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.540
You bastards are cops?

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:15.660
You're under arrest for
kidnapping and human trafficking.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:19.120
This fairy is a Semanian citizen.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.910
On your knees, hands above your heads.
Get to it.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:26.370
Damn it! You shithead cops set us up!

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.910
You've got quite the potty mouth, don't you?

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.870
Rick, read 'em their rights.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.750
You can do the honors, Kei.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.450
Alrighty, here we go.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.700
Listen carefully.
You have the right to remain silent.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.040
Anything that comes out
of that foul mouth of yours

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.200
may be used against you in a court of law.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.700
You have the right to a lawyer.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.700
If you can't afford to pay
one of those meddling shitheads,

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.580
you will be provided a public defender.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.040
So grateful you could cry, right?

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.830
Go to hell, pigs!

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.790
Hey...

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:11.750
Rick!

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:27.790
"You pathetically weak barbarians..."

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.080
"I'm taking the girl."

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.790
That's no Earth language... Farbani?

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:40.870
"The fairy was always meant to come to me."

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:43.950
Shut your damn mouth, alien...

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.660
Rick...

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.120
Rick!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.540
Damn it all!

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:04.620
Fifteen years ago, a hyperspace gate
appeared in the middle of the Pacific.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:09.910
Beyond the gate lay a strange world
filled with fairies and monsters.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:12.200
Kariaena Island. The city of San-Teresa.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.500
This city is Earth's "front door."

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.080
Over two million citizens
from this other world live here.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.540
A mixture of different races and
diverse cultures, haves and have-nots...

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:26.080
The world's newest "city of dreams."

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:30.450
But in the shadows of all this
chaos lurked countless crimes.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.290
Drugs. Prostitution. Weapons smuggling.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:39.540
The San-Teresa Metropolitan Police maintained
a special unit to deal with these crimes.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:13.660
Matoba, they found the perp's body.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.750
--No entry!
--It was lying on the road in Apple Hills.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:19.330
Apple Hills? That's two miles away.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:23.540
Chief Roth, I got three clean hits with a 9mm.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.250
No way in hell he made it that far.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.450
If he was a normal criminal, no.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.950
It was one of those goddamn aliens.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:37.790
So he was being controlled by
a Semanian wizard, you think?

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.580
The perp was speaking in Farbani.
Using vocab from their intellectual class.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.830
He said that fairy was special.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:49.370
I'll get things in order.
Matoba, you get some rest.

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:50.660
Not happening.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.450
My partner of four years was just killed.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.200
I'm gonna find him and make him pay.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.580
That's an order, Sergeant Matoba.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.370
I'm sorry about what happened to Rick.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:03.120
But that's why you need
to get some rest. Got it?

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:12.000
What the hell am I supposed to tell his wife?

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.200
I'll talk to her.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.950
No, I'll do it.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:22.040
I want your report on my desk
by 9:00 AM tomorrow.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.450
Roger.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.040
Shit!

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:55.080
Mister, I'll wash your car for you.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.450
It doesn't need washing.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.040
Don't say that.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.120
See?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:07.540
Three hundred dollars. If you don't pay it,
your car might get banged up.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:09.200
Money. Now.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.700
Scared, <i>doreany</i>?

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.620
Fine, fine. Calm down.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.000
Hurry up!

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.080
Now, where'd I put it?

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.290
There we go.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:21.500
Here.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.290
Pick it up. And appreciate it.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:25.410
You bastard...

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:35.120
You're Semanians, right?

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:40.290
Earth may be weak, but there are
scary people here. Remember that.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.620
Whatever...

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.500
"Yes, sir," you mean.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.120
Y-Yes, sir...

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:47.370
Get lost.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.370
Pathetic...

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.290
Okay, go! Go!

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:04.620
Oh, Kei! Rick's not home yet.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:06.540
Did something happen?

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:12.000
No... This can't be.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.160
I'm sorry.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.040
Hello?

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:39.790
About tomorrow...
There's been a change of plans.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:41.870
I need you to go meet a noble for me.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:43.790
What?

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:46.250
Go meet a noble.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:50.160
A VIP from the Farbani Kingdom
is arriving early tomorrow morning.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.250
You want me to go meet some alien noble?

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.540
That's a diplomat's job.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:58.910
We don't have enough detectives
who can speak their language.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:03.660
No thanks. Let me hunt down
the guy who killed Rick.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.200
The VIP might be involved in this.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.450
What?

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:13.370
Go get them.
I've already talked to the coast guard.

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.910
Bossy bastard...

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:19.910
Hey.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.040
We're almost to the gate.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.620
You ever been to their world?

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:38.000
Yup. I was in the military.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.160
In the war, huh?

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:45.910
I was stuffed inside a transport plane,
so I didn't get to see the gate itself.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:50.330
Nobody can see the Mirage Gate.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:53.330
We need to rely on information
from our observation satellites.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.540
But those damn aliens
can tell where the gate is

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:59.500
just by looking at the wind and tides.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:02.160
And do a damn sight better job than we can.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:06.330
And that's why the coast guard's always busy?

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:10.830
Yeah. If we wanted to catch all
the smugglers and illegal immigrants,

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:14.000
we'd need twice the funding and manpower.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:22.410
There they are.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:25.290
It's some important noble, right?

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:27.000
I'll let you deal with them.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.790
A child? A servant, maybe?

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.500
Where's the VIP?

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:00.500
Hey.

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:06.910
I am Exedilica, of the Knights of Mirvor.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:10.330
Do Earth sailors not even
have the ritual of welcoming?

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:16.370
Do you not know how to talk?

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.450
Um... no.

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:20.790
Then answer me. Well?

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:22.500
I didn't notice you.

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.540
I see.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:25.870
My name is

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:33.870
Tilarna Barsh Mirvor Imsedalya Iyeh
Tebreina Devol Nelano Seiya Nel Exedilica!

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.250
In your Earth language, that means

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:39.410
"Tilarna, eldest daughter of Seiya,
of the House of Exedilica,

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:44.540
heir to the bloodline of Duke Devol,
of the glorious Knights of Mirvor."

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:47.160
Now. What is your name?

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.500
Kei Matoba.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:51.250
What?

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.040
It's Kei Matoba.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.200
It's short.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:13:01.290
No, people of low birth often have short names.

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:02.950
I won't let it bother me.

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:06.950
I usually go by Tilarna Exedilica.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:14.290
Now, carry my things, Kay Imatuba.

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:16.080
Kei Matoba.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:18.620
I don't care. Start carrying.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:24.410
What?

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:27.620
Did you not hear me, Sergeant Matoba?

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.410
You'll be working with her from now on.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.950
You'll be doing your investigations with her.

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:35.830
She'll take Sergeant Fury's place.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:39.000
You want me to work with this alien?

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.580
That's racist, Sergeant Matoba!

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:46.830
I'm sorry. He doesn't understand
the circumstances.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.580
She came here to find that fairy.

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.040
She's a <i>fiel</i>.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:55.830
<i>Fiel queze badeley</i>. It means "most noble fairy."

00:13:55.830 --> 00:14:00.000
That fairy is the equivalent
of a VIP in the Semani world.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:05.080
It was kidnapped there
and brought here by smugglers.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:10.830
She's a Farbanian knight
sent here to recover the fairy.

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:13.120
That's correct, yes?

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.370
Correct.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.330
In accordance with our treaty with
the country called "The United Nations,"

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:22.000
the Knights of Mirvor are given
the right to dispense justice on Earth.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:28.450
I, Tilarna Exedilica, request your help
in the name of the Farbani Kingdom.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:34.200
This is bullshit! Rick was my partner
for four years, and now he's dead!

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:36.750
And now I'm supposed to babysit some kid?

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:38.160
This is an order.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:40.040
Your order can go eat shit!

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:45.160
Chief Roth, don't you want
to avenge Rick? This is just--

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:49.750
I've known Rick for 20 years.

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.580
I'm telling you to do this
because it's necessary.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.660
Do you need any more explanation than that?

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.120
But...

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.450
It appears that my own will is being ignored.

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:04.620
I want to work with the best "boliceman"
your city has to offer.

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:08.790
I can't imagine a rude boor
like this acting as my guard.

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:12.700
Oh, I'm sorry. We can find another...

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:15.830
No, he'll be your partner.

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:17.580
Or do you want a man

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:20.120
whose etiquette is perfect,
but who's otherwise completely useless?

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.660
Inspector Roth...

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:25.540
If so, I don't think you'll
be getting your fairy back.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.750
Don't touch it.

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:50.830
Don't touch it.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:01.660
I said don't touch it.

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:10.410
What've we got, Tony?

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:14.500
He talked. He was too scared
to say much, though.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:17.830
That fairy was stolen, supposedly.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:21.700
From a gang of Mexicans in a Ridgeline.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:23.830
Sounds like he doesn't know their names.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:24.830
Thanks.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.830
What?

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:30.790
Nothing. Let's go.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:43.160
So? Where are we going?

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:46.040
We're going to find the fairy's original owners.

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:50.950
There can't be that many Mexican gangs
in Ridgelines running around.

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:52.660
What's a Ridgeline?

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:53.620
A car.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:54.870
What's a Mexican?

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:56.450
A person from Mexico.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:57.450
What's a gang?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:01.410
Enough. Just shut up and sit there.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.870
What's this?

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:03.870
No!

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:10.580
<i>Rakebye</i>! Are you trying to get me killed?

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:13.870
Please, just don't do anything!
Don't touch anything!

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:17.200
Wait here.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.290
I'm not taking orders from you.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:22.040
I'm going with you, Kay Imatuba.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.330
Fine, whatever.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:27.290
Just try to walk as far away
from me as possible.

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:29.040
I don't want anyone thinking we're friends.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.290
What a coincidence. Neither do I.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:37.120
Hey, we don't open until seven.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:39.750
Oh, Mr. Matoba.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:42.370
Kenny, is O'Neill in?

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:45.500
He's in the other room on the phone.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.450
Hey, that's an alien!

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.870
I hate those guys!

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.540
Have a good time with her, then.
I'm going in.

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:57.950
Hold it, missy.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:17:58.910
What?

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:02.370
He can go in, but you're not welcome.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:09.200
Hey, did you not hear me? Turn around and...

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:15.830
Turn around and what?

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:17.910
Go on in, miss.

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:18.950
Very good.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:26.540
Did you think I'd get scared and beg for help?

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:31.700
Yes, this should be a good deal for us both.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:37.080
This gift of 50 51-inch TVs
brought to us by these sinful

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:40.910
young children is truly a blessing from God.
For the Lord sayeth...

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:47.410
There are no TVs.
It's a theological analogy for God's grace.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:51.250
Oh, I've got visitors.
Blessings of God be with you!

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:56.080
Sergeant Matoba!
Feeling the breath of God today?

00:18:56.080 --> 00:19:01.910
And who's the beautiful lady with you?
Welcome to my house of faith!

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:03.250
Want something to drink?

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:07.540
O'Neill, I'm looking for a Mexican gang.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:11.950
They drive a Ridgeline.
Probably transporters. Know anything?

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:17.620
They're a violent bunch, and I'd rather
not anger them if possible...

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:18.910
So you do know something.

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:20.660
It's impossible to say!

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:25.540
But perhaps a sufficiently large
donation could make God

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:27.200
whisper something to me...

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:30.120
A donation of around
300 dollars, specifically.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:31.580
If you don't know anything,

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.500
you'll have to deal with
the goddess of the courtroom

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:35.790
and her sword and scales.

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:37.250
You're on probation, aren't you?

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.200
That's an illegal threat, Sergeant Matoba!

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:43.620
Someday Satan will get his claws into your soul!

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:48.040
Satan can suck my dick.
Now, what's this about 51-inch TVs?

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.700
Maybe I should go ask the guys
in the burglary division?

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:55.450
You're willing to believe the words of a thief?

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:57.080
He's an informant.

00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:58.700
But he's a thief.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:04.660
O'Neill may be a criminal,
but he doesn't like drugs or murder.

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:07.040
He can be trusted... to a degree.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:10.160
He's a guy you just can't hate, I guess.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:15.250
I don't understand. Aren't you supposed
to be enforcers of justice?

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:17.120
Well...

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:21.410
I was told that there were warriors on Earth
who fought for the cause of justice.

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:25.040
That they helped the needy and fought evil.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:27.660
That's what you "bolicemen" are, right?

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:29.870
I honestly had some hopes for you.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:34.830
But I can't believe you're
making deals with a thief.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.950
Do you have no pride?

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:44.450
It's complicated.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:45.500
What is?

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:46.870
A lot of stuff.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:49.500
In the old days, you'd be right, but now...

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:51.410
It's really complicated.

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:53.160
I don't understand.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.700
Nobody does.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:03.330
581 Mason Street. Room 603.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:06.790
Antonio Alvarez. You need backup?

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:11.200
Nope. If there's no word from me in 30 minutes,
then you can worry about me.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.370
Roger. Be careful.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:15.370
Thanks.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:16.700
You stay here...

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:20.000
Yeah, I should've known you wouldn't listen.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:21.120
Of course not.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:24.750
Don't touch anything.

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:26.370
No, it's the smell.

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:28.450
The smell?

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.830
The smell of <i>latena</i>.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:36.870
Someone controlled by
an evil wizard was just here...

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:38.370
What are you talking about?

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:39.540
The enemy's close!

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:43.450
"Shield of law, protection of the war god."

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.370
Follow me!

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:50.620
Hey, wait!

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:56.660
Don't move! This is the police!

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:02.410
Get down!

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:08.540
Crap!

00:23:41.950 --> 00:23:42.750
"Next time"

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:44.580
Next time on <i>COP CRAFT</i>.
